// The "returns fresh" bits of a summary. Bit 30 is set when the function may
// hand back a block that something else holds: a parameter, a block it stored
// in an export or a list, a literal string. It is clear when every path
// returns a block this very call made and nothing else names, which is what
// lets a caller own the result (`ys = f()`). Bit 31, the sign, is set unless
// the elements are the result's alone as well (esc_deep_ret), which is what
// lets a caller free a list of lists with them. Only a function that returns a
// list, a struct or a string has the question asked; for any other return type
// both bits are clear and mean nothing.
//
// A function is fresh when its return clause is a list literal, or a name this
// function owns (own/query.id, with the return clause itself not counted as a
// use), and every early `return` hands back a list literal. An owned string
// holds heap copies only (own/str/), so the same test serves strings.

esc_nf(int fn) {
  int enf = 0;
  if(esc_heap_ty((import ns2)[fn]) == 1) {
    enf = esc_nf_bits(fn);
  }
} return int enf;
